6. How it's built

The single most important decision: every screen reads through one function, services/api.ts. No component embeds a data array. In mock mode it queries the in-browser engine; in API mode it calls FastAPI and falls back automatically if the backend is down.

That one seam buys you: real data can replace seed data with zero UI changes; the demo can't break in front of judges; and swapping in PostGIS is a change in one module.

The synthetic data engine is deterministic (seeded mulberry32 PRNG) — the same seed always produces the same dataset. Scales from 400 projects up to 1,500 projects / 100k parcels / 50k documents / 50k beneficiaries, switchable at runtime.

The risk model is a transparent weighted-factor model, not a black box. Ten named factors with declared weights (22, 19, 14, 12, 10, 9, 8, 6, 6, 4). This is a deliberate accuracy trade — a gradient-boosted model would score better and be unusable, because the output isn't a prediction, it's an argument an officer must defend to an auditor.

